{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the outcomes of each lottery and considers differences between outcomes as negligible. This implies that the actual monetary amounts (5 EUR vs. 5000 EUR) are treated as not meaningfully different in value to the decision maker. Given this, the reason instructs choosing the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. In this case, Lottery A offers 5 EUR with 100% probability, while Lottery B offers 5000 EUR with 0.1% probability and 0 EUR with 99.9% probability. If the outcomes are considered negligible in difference, then the relevant comparison is probabilities: Lottery A has a 100% chance of a positive outcome, Lottery B only 0.1%. Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery A.",
